From 578841f24d0f1156fc761a46c492959e7d20fa4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaxorcist <vaxorcist@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:30:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RB730: DEC disk layout, sim_disk, status, seek and range
 fixes, one RB80

Fixes for the RB730 disk controller of the VAX-11/730 (RB02 = RL02,
RB80 = R80), each tested with VMS V3.5 on the 730 and, for the RB02,
with the same cartridge on the RL11 of a VAX-11/750:

- Disk images in DEC logical block order (cylinder, head, sector).  The
  images were stored head by head, so RB02 images were neither binary
  copies of a cartridge nor interchangeable with RL02 images of the RL11
  although DEC's drivers put a block on the same cylinder, head and
  sector on both controllers.  SET RBn LAYOUT=OLD (before ATTACH) keeps
  images of earlier versions usable for the time being.
- The RB80 has 31 sectors per track, as DEC's drivers use it (242,606
  blocks, the RM80's capacity; sector 31 was never used), so RB80
  images are in logical block order too; LAYOUT=OLD keeps 32.
- Uses the SIMH disk library (sim_disk): SIMH, VHD and RAW formats,
  SET RBn FORMAT, autosize between RB02 and RB80, metadata, DISK debug,
  bad block table on new images, file system detection; DEV_DISK.
- GET STATUS of an RB02 reports the drive status bits (an operator
  precedence error dropped them); READ HEADER returns the current
  cylinder and head.
- A drive without a cartridge is not ready and ends commands with drive
  error, so VMS reports the medium offline instead of a controller or
  parity error.
- A finishing seek raises its own drive's attention and only executes
  the controller's current command if that is for the same drive (it
  could run another drive's command on the seeking drive).
- Range checks: a seek stops at the last cylinder, a transfer to a
  track beyond the last head fails with header error.
- At most one RB80, as on the IDC (one R80 and up to three RL02,
  EK-RB730-TD-001 figure 3-2): SET RBn RB80 (also by autosize) is
  refused while another unit is the RB80.
- HELP RB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
